analysis:
This batch contains only test files. GenerationLoopExitThinkingServingTests.swift (head 1-376) and GenerationLoopExitThinkingTests.swift (head 1-250) are new. They exercise a loop-guard exit-thinking feature for Gemma 4. When the guard detects a loop inside the thought, it cancels the row. It then submits a continuation whose prompt is the original prompt plus every produced token plus the channel-close marker, with maxTokens reduced accordingly (Serving 280-287).

The tests also cover:
- usage accounting across both rows (completionTokens = first output + 1 + continuation);
- the case where no budget is left (303-316);
- policy default model types (gemma4 only);
- logprobs disabling the exit;
- the DARKBLOOM_LOOP_EXIT_THINKING env override;
- launchd passthrough of the env keys (Tests 231-237);
- row-release waiting;
- atomic admission against a first-content deadline with GlobalKVCacheBudget (339-366).

The MiMoV26EncodedMediaIngressTests change replaces a polling wait with a removal-hook expectation for media reservation settlement (head 343-347, 380). It still asserts a zero reservation count, so no leak check is weakened.

No production source is in this batch, so no regression is cited. Integration should verify the production implementation of GenerationLoopExitThinking / EngineV2Bridge continuation for the following:
- (a) Billing/usage (A-009): continuation tokens count once and the budget cannot exceed the request's maxTokens.
- (b) The continuation reuses the same cacheSalt/scope, with no cross-tenant prefix-cache reuse (T-041), and does not create an SSD donation outside the scope.
- (c) Serving-slot/KV reservation release on cancel before the continuation (A-018, T-010).
- (d) Encryption fail-closed on the continuation's response path (T-008).
- (e) The env passthrough adds operator-only knobs; the operator is already trusted over local config (TB-003).
